    {
      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "National average gas price jumps 15 cents to $4.09/gallon.",
      "details": "The national average price for a gallon of regular gasoline increased by 15 cents from the previous week, reaching $4.09. This surge pushed most states to an average of $4 per gallon or higher. The increase was attributed to rising crude oil prices, driven by volatility along the Strait of Hormuz and instability in the region, which pushed crude oil prices into the $90 per barrel range. This significant increase in a discretionary spending input like gas prices likely suppressed consumer spending on non-essential items, leading to lower ROAS and higher CPA for a DTC food gifting brand.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-31",
      "description": "U. of Michigan Consumer Sentiment rises to 55.2, a five-month high.",
      "details": "The University of Michigan Consumer Sentiment Index's final reading for July rose to 55.2, an 11.5% increase from June, marking a five-month high. This improvement was largely driven by easing gas prices earlier in the month and broad-based improvements across various demographic groups. Despite the gain, overall sentiment remained historically depressed. Improved consumer confidence can lead to a boost in discretionary spending, positively impacting ROAS and lowering CPA for a DTC food gifting brand.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "boosts_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "University of Michigan"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-02",
      "description": "National Friendship Day celebrates platonic bonds in the US.",
      "details": "National Friendship Day is observed annually on the first Sunday of August in the United States, falling on August 2nd in 2026. This day encourages people to connect with friends and celebrate the value of companionship. As a gifting-heavy brand, this occasion could inspire consumers to purchase gifts for friends, potentially boosting ROAS and lowering CPA.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "seasonal",
      "icon": "🗓️",
      "mood_impact": "boosts_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "National Day Calendar"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-07",
      "description": "US economy loses 23,000 jobs in July; unemployment rate dips to 4.1%.",
      "details": "The US Bureau of Labor Statistics reported that nonfarm payroll employment decreased by 23,000 in July, contrary to expectations for job growth. The unemployment rate, however, dipped slightly to 4.1% from 4.2% in June, primarily because people left the labor force. This unexpected job loss, coupled with a shrinking labor force, signals economic weakness and potential consumer anxiety. Such news typically suppresses discretionary spending, leading to lower ROAS and higher CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "Bureau of Labor Statistics"
    },
    {
